{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/69239-the-call-and-relics-from-storyteller-s-handbook","id":69239,"title":"The Call and Relics (from Storyteller's Handbook)","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mummy: The Curse"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-02-10T11:23:08-08:00","id":69239,"title":"The Call and Relics (from Storyteller's Handbook)","content":"So on page 214 it mentions how Cults using a Mummy's relics can perform the Call without permanently destroying a Relic...at the expense of all of its Sekhem, rendering it useless for the duration.<br /> <br /> Does this relic have to be a relic purchased with the Relic Merit? If so, doesn't this seem ...mean? The Relic isn't gone, which is good, but the Player doesn't have access to it for at minimum 4 weeks, at maximum 26. Let's say on average a 2-dot Relic is drained for 15 weeks. That's a long time that the player doesn't have access to something that they explicitly paid for. I can see why &quot;we had to sacrifice a relic to summon you&quot; makes sense from a lore standpoint, but as a Player I don't care because I never spent any points on it, which takes the edge off of the &quot;sacrifice&quot;.<br /> <br /> I mean, I get that Mummies are already powerful enough, and you get your stuff eventually when you really need it the most, but it seems irritatingly punitive to me. The only way around it that I have noticed is the Piece of Life Tomb Endowment.<br /> <br /> Am I misreading how the Call works or do you think this is intentional?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=484226#post484226\" target=\"_blank\">Nihhina kalekal-zidu kal masun, kal manudanadu. Nihhina kalekal-zidu nukal shaghu-desasudu \u2014 nihhina kalekal-zidu kal innu-desasudu udhkal samm</a>.&quot; Arthur Ashe<br /> She/her, contributing writer for <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/363404/Scion-Pride-2021\" target=\"_blank\">Scion: Pride 2021</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1923-bigdamnhero","name":"BigDamnHero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1923_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1263"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-10T18:33:28-08:00","id":69532,"title":"","content":"I think it's intentional. These are the prices that must be paid.<br /> <br /> If I were using a cult summoning to kick off a new campaign without a single session having been played yet, then I would probably say that the cult stole a relic (from a museum, or another Mummy's tomb), sacrificed an 'unpurchased' relic or more likely an 'unpurchased' vestige, or that there is a sorcerer in the cult who cast a spell to awaken the Mummy. While there are no hard-fast rules yet for mortal sorcerers specific to Mummy, the books mention how they can call a Mummy or even summon amkhata, so there is precedent.<br /> <br /> If it were mid-campaign and the PC's Sekhem dropped like a rock or they died, then I'd be more likely to put their own relic temporarily out of service. Mostly because, at that point, I hope the player understands the need for the story and drama, after we've had some time invested into it.<br /> <br /> You don't want to open a brand new campaign with, &quot;Your cult awakens you. By the way, your 4-dot relic is out of commission.&quot; Do what's fun for you and your players","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/638-reseru","name":"reseru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar638_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1574"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}